# Photography platform

Next.js App Router in `src/`, Supabase Auth + Postgres, private S3 (`masters/` raw, `proofs/` watermarked), CloudFront for `proofs/*` only, watermark Lambda in `aws/lambda/watermark/`, Stripe Checkout. Orient from `docs/REPO_MAP.md`.

## Security

1. Issue short-lived S3 pre-signed PUT/GET URLs. Never proxy photo bytes through Next.js routes.
2. Never put `masters/*` on CloudFront, in public URLs, or in client bundles. Masters are time-limited pre-signed GETs after a server-side entitlement check.
3. Update order status and download quotas only in `/api/stripe/webhook` after verifying `Stripe-Signature`. Ignore client redirects.
4. RLS on every table, and `profiles.role === 'admin'` via `verifyAdmin()` on admin API routes and actions.
5. `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, and `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` stay server-side. Never import `src/lib/supabase/admin.ts` from a `'use client'` file.
6. Watermark in Lambda. CSS `contextmenu` / `user-select` are secondary only.

## Token & Search Discipline

1. Read `docs/REPO_MAP.md` first. Do not broad-search the repo or list directories to orient.
2. If the user `@`-mentions files, edit those files first. Search elsewhere only for an exact missing symbol, with a targeted grep or symbol lookup.
3. Read only the relevant line ranges of large files. Do not re-read a file already loaded in this chat unless it changed.
4. After adding or renaming routes, DB columns, or `src/lib/` exports, update `docs/REPO_MAP.md` in 1–2 lines.
5. Run `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run lint` once at the end of a task, not after every small edit. Keep verification output concise.
